# Reviewed, expiring Trivy vulnerability exceptions for the Release workflow
# (.github/workflows/ship.yml). Passed explicitly with --ignorefile to the
# HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability scan only; the secret scan never reads it.
#
# Policy (owner decision): every new HIGH or CRITICAL finding fails the run,
# except an entry below that a reviewed pull request added. Each entry is
#
#   # reason: <10 to 200 characters: why it is safe to ship, and the fix plan>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# (or a GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx identifier). The reason line sits in the comment
# block directly above its entry. exp: is Trivy's own syntax: after that date
# Trivy stops honouring the entry, and release/deployment/trivy_policy.py
# fails every run until a reviewed PR removes or renews it. The date must be
# after today and at most 90 days ahead. No duplicates, at most 50 entries,
# ASCII with LF line endings. Secret findings can never be excepted.
#
# This file starts with no entries.
